# Build the reactor in parallel — one thread per available core.
#
# The 29 modules form a narrow critical path (vance-api -> vance-shared ->
# vance-brain) with 13 addons hanging off the end that are independent of each
# other. Sequentially that costs ~2:54 for a full `mvn clean install`; with -T
# it drops to ~1:27 on an 18-core machine, and the addons' pnpm/vite builds
# (exec-maven-plugin, prepare-package) overlap with Java work instead of adding
# their ~49s on top.
#
# 1C scales with the machine, so CI runners with fewer cores degrade gracefully
# rather than oversubscribing.
#
# Lives here rather than in ./wb so direct `mvn` calls and IDE builds get it
# too. Does not reach qa/ — that reactor sits outside this directory and keeps
# running serially, which is what its Mongo-container tests need.
-T 1C
